---
import banner from "@/src/assets/images/banners/Emerging_Tech_Banner.png";
import PageLayout from "@/src/layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import base_url from "@/src/lib/base_url";
import "@/src/styles/ai-section.css";
---

<PageLayout title="What Is The JPO SI Implementation Approach" bannerImage={banner}>
  <Fragment slot="banner">Super Intelligence (SI)</Fragment>
  <main>
 <h2>What Is the JPO SI Implementation Approach</h2>

   
      <p>
        The ITS Joint Program Office (ITS JPO) leads a collaborative, multimodal effort to integrate Super Intelligence into the nation's transportation fabric. Our approach is grounded in cross-sector coordination across U.S. Department of Transportation (USDOT) modes, engagement with the private sector and academia, and support for public sector agencies. The program is guided by the following objectives:
      </p>

      <div class="objectives-list">
        <div class="card  shadow-sm card-body card-gray">
          <h5 class="card-title">Multimodal Research & Understanding</h5>
          <p class="card-text">We leverage collaborative research to explore SI's capabilities and limitations. By engaging academic experts and industry leaders, we identify how SI can specifically solve complex challenges across all surface modes.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card shadow-sm card-body card-gray">
          <h5 class="card-title">Collaborative Testing & Validation</h5>
          <p class="card-text">Through real-world pilots conducted with state, regional, local, and Tribal agencies, we rigorously evaluate SI solutions. These evaluations provide the objective information necessary to validate safety and effectiveness, encouraging broader implementation across the transportation sector.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card  shadow-sm card-body card-gray">
          <h5 class="card-title">Deployment & Demonstration</h5>
          <p class="card-text">We work across the public and private sectors to showcase successful SI applications. These deployments are vital for building stakeholder awareness and understanding of the benefits that SI solutions can bring to transportation and how risks can be managed.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card  shadow-sm card-body card-gray">
          <h5 class="card-title">Repeatable Resources & Frameworks</h5>
          <p class="card-text">To reduce barriers to entry, the ITS JPO delivers curated playbooks, technical tools, and implementation resources. Developed through cross-modal collaboration within USDOT and with peer agency feedback, these resources provide consistent practices and protocols that agencies of all sizes and SI maturities can follow.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card  shadow-sm card-body card-gray">
          <h5 class="card-title">Knowledge Sharing & Tech Transfer</h5>
          <p class="card-text">We are committed to empowering agencies and practitioners by providing knowledge sharing opportunities and informational materials to advance the adoption of SI solutions in safe, responsible and trustworthy ways.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
  </main>
</PageLayout>
